## Origin

**Decision (Deepak Pai, 9 Oct 2026):** story 8.6 (budget-vs-actual column on Numbers) leaves konsol#305 Delivery 2 and becomes this epic. Rejected: building 8.6 inside D2. Recorded on #305.

The full plan, with file:line references and live counts, is in `bench-15/archive/budget-epic/plan.md`.

## Goal

A group accountant sees the **approved** budget next to consolidated actuals on Numbers:
- the same headings, presentation currency and group scope;
- Budget and Variance-to-budget columns, plus a YTD budget on the P&L;
- a drill from a heading to entity and account, showing the rate used;
- the budget in the 8.5 xlsx export;
- a visible "no approved budget" state, never a blank column.

Later, outside 8.6: entity-level BvA translated, favourability (konsolidat#214), forecast (#106), Excel reads.

## Measured state (konsol `ac5cc5fa`, konsolidat `3246d0e`, local stack 9 Oct)

- **Budget intake exists, outside D365, but has never been used.** Three paths reach the warehouse:
  - Budget Cycle → Sheet → Line, synced to `budget_monthly_input` on cycle submit;
  - REST / Excel `budget_save`, `budget_save_batch`, `budget_cell_save`;
  - Budget Annual Input plus Spread Profile, synced on every save.
- **None of them has ever carried a row.** Budget Cycle, Sheet, Line and Annual Input: 0 rows. Every ClickHouse budget table: 0 rows. This corrects the D2 recon, which said "no budget intake".
- **No model translates or consolidates budget.** Every budget model is at entity grain, with no currency, no rate and no elimination. Numbers reads only `gold_fully_consolidated_tb`.
- **`gold_variance_analysis` holds actuals only.** It has 37,523 rows, all with `budget_scenario_id = ''`, and 0 have a budget amount.
- **No budget rate exists.** Group Exchange Rate offers `Closing` / `Average` only, with no scenario key. Rates reach 2025 P12; actuals reach 2025 P07.
- **Budgets assume 12 periods.** Budget Line has 12 fixed columns, the API clamps periods to 1-12, and `assert_spread_has_12_periods` demands 12 (#210).
- **Two more undeclared items:**
  - a budget has no currency;
  - `main_account` is free text (Data), not a Link.
- **Approval is not uniform.** Annual Input reaches the warehouse **before** its cycle is approved; sheets reach it only on submit.
- **D365 coupling:**
  - Budget Cycle's write-back enqueue and Budget Sheet's `d365_*` fields stay as they are (frozen);
  - `silver_budget_entries` and the `'BUDGET'` branch of `gold_scenario_trial_balance` are ERP tree (konsolidat#221 / #235). They are not repaired here and not read by new work.
- **Tests that cannot fail.** 10 budget and variance assertions are green with 0 budget rows.

## Owned elsewhere: do not touch

- **#287** (the other session):
  - part 1 merged in #343 on 7 Oct (budget DDL and Annual Input dimensions declared);
  - still open there: `_LEGACY_DIM_MAP` together with the Excel add-in's fixed dimension arguments; Budget Cost Center (generalise or retire); the `dim_` rule for `in_budget`.
- **#282:** `reconcile_all` misses `budget_monthly_input`. It is a **prerequisite** here; who builds it is still to agree.

## Decisions needed before building (options in the plan; none made)

- **BUD-1 Intake:**
  - BUD-1-1: budget CSV like the TB upload;
  - BUD-1-2: existing paths only;
  - BUD-1-3: CSV canonical, existing paths kept;
  - BUD-1-4: group entry in the close app.
- **BUD-2 Grain:**
  - BUD-2-1: entity budgets, translated and consolidated;
  - BUD-2-2: group budget at account level, in presentation currency;
  - BUD-2-3: group budget at heading level;
  - BUD-2-4: entity budgets plus group budget adjustments.
- **BUD-3 Translation rate:**
  - BUD-3-1: declared budget rate, effective-dated;
  - BUD-3-2: the period's actual rates;
  - BUD-3-3: both, with an FX-effect split;
  - BUD-3-4: a required policy on the cycle.
- **BUD-4 Which budget is "approved":**
  - BUD-4-1: the active budget scenario with a submitted cycle;
  - BUD-4-2: declared per group and year;
  - BUD-4-3: the user picks.
  - Also: sum of layers or board layer only; gating Annual Input; forecast.
- **BUD-5 Eliminations:**
  - BUD-5-1: none, declared;
  - BUD-5-2: IC partner on budget lines plus the IC rules;
  - BUD-5-3: manual group budget eliminations.
- **BUD-6 Scope:**
  - BUD-6-1: P&L only;
  - BUD-6-2: P&L and BS;
  - BUD-6-3: P&L now, BS later behind a flag.
- **BUD-7 Sign:**
  - BUD-7-1: signed like actuals;
  - BUD-7-2: magnitudes, signed by `normal_balance` in one model.
  - Favourability: BUD-7-a, three states, or BUD-7-b, left out (konsolidat#174, #214).
- **BUD-8 Dimensions:**
  - BUD-8-1: dimensionless column;
  - BUD-8-2: budget dimensions ⊆ TB dimensions;
  - BUD-8-3: left to #287.
- **BUD-9 Approver:**
  - BUD-9-1: close roles (Analyst drafts, Admin submits), Budget* roles retired;
  - BUD-9-2: the four layer roles kept;
  - BUD-9-3: layers as data, single Admin approval.
- **BUD-10 Period shape (#210):**
  - BUD-10-1: tall lines on the declared calendar;
  - BUD-10-2: 12 columns, other calendars refused;
  - BUD-10-3: columns generated from the calendar.
- **BUD-11 Signature:**
  - BUD-11-1: budget outside the close signature;
  - BUD-11-2: budget fingerprinted.

## Stages (rough)

| stage | repo | rows |
|---|---|---|
| S0 decide BUD-1..11 (HMD tables, recorded with provenance) | none | 0 |
| S1 prerequisites: #282, Annual Input gated, account Link, fixtures so budget tests can fail | konsol | 5-7 |
| S2 intake: currency, period shape, sign, CSV, roles | konsol | 10-14 |
| S3 budget fact: currency and sign carried, per declared period, never reading ERP models | konsolidat | 5-7 |
| S4 translated and consolidated budget, a model of its own (the actuals rate guard raises on a missing rate) | konsolidat (+ konsol rate input) | 8-12 |
| S5 Numbers columns, drill, xlsx, "no approved budget" state | konsol | 8-10 |
| S6 beyond 8.6: entity BvA, favourability, forecast, Excel | both | separate |

- **To 8.6:** about 36-50 rows. A group-level grain (BUD-2-2 or BUD-2-3) cuts it to about 25-30, without an entity drill.
- **Delivery:** konsolidat work ships as paired PRs with a column-contract pin test.
- **Upgrade path:** every budget table is empty today, so shape changes are idempotent no-op patches. A site with rows gets a pivot patch, and is refused (not defaulted) where a currency is missing.

